    {
      "id": 50043,
      "kind": "compute",
      "difficulty": 55,
      "prompt": "A nonzero vector D has norm 5. What is the norm of −2D?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "text": "−10",
          "value": "-10"
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "text": "5",
          "value": "5"
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "text": "25",
          "value": "25"
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "text": "10",
          "value": "10"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "D",
      "solution": "Norms are nonnegative: ||−2D|| = |−2| ||D|| = 10. Negative scaling changes direction, not the sign of length.",
